course: dictionary
lesson: 11377
title: The word abrade
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Abrade is a tricky word, but its context gives you clues. «The rough rope abraded his hands.» Rope that rubs against your hands again and again will wear the skin away, so abrade must mean to scrape or wear away a surface by rubbing.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The rough rope scraped his hands» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Abrade is also a science word. «Sand carried by the river abraded the rocks over thousands of years.» Rivers, waves and ice carry grit that slowly wears rock away, and this wearing away is called abrasion.
fact: Abrade is a verb: abrade, abrades, abraded, abrading.
fact: «Abrade» means to scrape or wear away the surface of something by rubbing.
fact: «Abraded» means scraped or worn away, as in «abraded skin».
fact: Sand, pebbles and ice can abrade rocks, and the wearing away of rock this way is called abrasion.
fact: An abraded knee is a graze, and sandpaper abrades wood to make it smooth.
exercise: «The sandpaper abraded the rough wood until it was smooth.» What does abraded mean? | *Scraped away by rubbing | Cut into pieces with a saw | Painted in bright colours | Soaked in water
exercise: Which of these can abrade a rock over many years? | A feather floating on a lake | *Sand carried by a river | A soft cloud | A sunbeam on a hill
exercise: «The fall left a deep, abraded graze on her knee.» Find and copy the word that means scraped by rubbing. | deep | knee | *abraded | fall
test: «The rough rope abraded his hands.» Which word is closest in meaning to abrade? | Polish | Tie | Lift | *Scrape away
test: A child asks, «Does abrade mean to paint something?» What is the answer? | *No, it means to wear away a surface by rubbing | No, it means to build a wall | Yes, it means to make something dry quickly | Yes, it means to cover a surface with paint
exam: «The waves and sand abraded the cliff, but the cliff still stood tall.» What happened to the cliff? | It was painted bright blue | It grew taller every year | *Its surface was worn away by rubbing | It was built from wood
